WEBVTT

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.850
Looks like your injuries have completely 
healed, Adam Muirhead.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.720
Oh? So his name is Adam...

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.570
Thanks to the stress of having to 
watch this squirt fight,

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.460
it took longer than expected, 
but yes.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.970
Good.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:22.870
Then I order you, Jack the Ripper, to return 
to your original unit, the Second Platoon.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.710
Aye aye.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.000
Ogura Sio.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.260
Uh... yes!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.900
I'm assigning you to the 
Second Platoon, as well.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.880
Yes— Huh?!

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.490
Take care of her, Jack.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.990
Aye aye...

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.280
Strange. I thought you'd be against it.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.070
Nobunagun's assignment?

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.210
Oh, I don't really approve.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.810
She doesn't know the first 
thing about sniping.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:53.850
So then why...?

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.080
It's just that she's got 
unrivaled battle smarts.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.330
I don't want to admit it, 
but it's true.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.580
I see. So we share the same 
view on this matter.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.310
Yes.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.680
Rather than put her in a 
specialized sniping squad,

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.960
we'll have her prove her 
worth on a combat team.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:23.100
Abilities of distinguished individuals, 
numerous throughout history,

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.390
have been stored in special E-genes.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.390
<b>E-genes</b>

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.250
The E-gene holders, 
who inherit those genes,

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.730
<b>AU balls</b>

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:34.760
summon the abilities sleeping 
within them via AU balls,

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.350
and embody AU weapons.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:44.020
The E-gene holders belonging to the 
supranational organization Dogoo

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.070
versus enemies from outer space 
known as Evolutionary Invasion Objects.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.660
This is the chronicle of their 
fateful battle for humanity!

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:26.740
Gun No. 5: The Second Platoon!

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:32.640
Miss Ogura, you can see it now!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.670
That's the base you'll be stationed at 
as part of the Second Platoon,

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:46.830
<b>Alex Logan </b>

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.700
<i>Alex Logan.</i>

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.660
It's huuuuge!

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.380
Photo op, photo op!

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.420
Quit spazzing, Squirt.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.290
What's with the grumpy face?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.740
W-Whadaya mean?!

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.270
Didja get butterflies during 
your first mission?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.980
Th-This is wrong! I have Asao...

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:08.610
Let's go!

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.670
If you drag your feet, I'll leave you behind.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.390
W-Wait up!

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.780
The hell are you doing?!

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.360
Welcome back, Jack!

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.650
Gandhi. Newton.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.810
Yo! Welcome back.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.790
And welcome to the 
Second Platoon, Nobunagun.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.320
Th-Thank you!

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.440
Allow me to reintroduce myself.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.280
I'm Mahesh Mirza. My E-gene is Gandhi.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.550
Ah, the barrier guy.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.770
Don't say "barrier." 
It's so lame.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.220
And this is...

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.330
W-W-W-W-W-W-Wha?!

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.960
This is Jess Beckham— you know, Newton.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.520
I-It's not like I'm sh-shocked, or anything!

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.490
Doesn't matter to me who he... 
you know, kisses, or...

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:13.180
O-Oh yeah! Plus she's a foreigner! 
Could totally be a greeting!

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:16.370
...Or not. Not like that, it's not.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:20.950
B-But it has nothing to do with me! 
Nothing at all...

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.260
Long time no see...

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.920
Whaaaaaat?!

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.730
W-W-W-Wait! Wait! Wait!

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:32.350
Nngh, so soft.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:36.430
No! This is... her tongue? Her tongue?!

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.170
Creeping slimily along my gums...

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.100
Her breath, through her nose, is crazy... 
This is so embarrassing!

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:46.070
What the heck is going on?!

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.220
What the hell. What the hell.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.290
Seriously, what the hell!

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.590
Jack the Ripper, that piece of shit.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.700
He destroyed four major organs!

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.730
Why can't he think of things from the 
dissector's point of view?!

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:05.110
Oh, don't be that way, John Hunter.

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:08.800
There's no way to keep track of 
stuff like that in combat.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.000
Vidocq.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.310
Those guys who just have to kill 
stuff have it so easy.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:16.320
Quit your griping.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:21.380
More importantly, the brain is intact, right? 
Can you open it up and lemme have a look?

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.960
Brain tissue? Got something in mind?

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:28.930
Seems to be a preoccupation ever 
since the Saipan incident,

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:31.620
of my easy chair, here.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.080
Then let's get to it.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:40.490
We'll take a good hard look and 
make our deductions, Vidocq.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.490
Dogoo has three cruiser strongholds:

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.550
the one we're on now,

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.260
<i>Alex Logan,</i>

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.340
<b>Alex Logan </b>

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.600
<b>George Atsumi</b>

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:53.600
<i>George Atsumi,</i>

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.310
<b>Steven Hiller</b>

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.260
and <i>Steven Hiller.</i>

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:01.770
<b>Clayton Forrester</b>

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:01.470
And finally, there's also the 
<i>Clayton Forrester</i> on special duty.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:02.400
<b>Alex Logan</b>

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.720
Two platoons of holder combatants are 
stationed on each cruiser,

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.900
<b>First Platoon </b>

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.900
<b>Second Platoon </b>

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:10.790
and they patrol over the Pacific Ocean. 
When an Evolutionary Invasion Object appears,

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:15.840
the closest stronghold's 
platoons descend to fight it.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:20.590
So I guess... that's it for the explanation 
of platoons and strongholds, but...

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.060
...are you okay?

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:23.990
Y-Yessir!

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.180
I'm back!

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.660
Oh! Galiko, I was waiting for you.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:37.870
That's "Galileo."

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:41.300
Oh, shush. "Galiko" is plenty for 
a pipsqueak like you.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.660
Awww yeah, just what I wanted:

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.850
Baked noodles on the bread.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:50.240
Japanese people come up 
with the coolest stuff! 

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.150
<b>Yakisoba bread </b>

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:56.840
Whatsa matter, Galiko?

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.600
Nothing...

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.840
Hmm. Yeah. It's weird.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.230
Hey, Galiko!

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:10.460
Y-Yes?!

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:15.380
During the Taiwan incident, you were observing 
the Invasion Object from the water, right?

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:18.070
Can you show me the data on 
the one that self-destructed...

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:21.920
...and also the recording of 
the Sixth Platoon?

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:24.400
Y-Yes! I'd be happy to!

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:29.040
Next, I'll introduce you to the 
facilities on <i>Alex Logan.</i>

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:30.340
O-Okay!

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.620
This is the meeting room.

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:36.900
And the training room. 
You can use it at your leisure.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:41.420
This is the reference room. You can check 
documentation related to E-genes.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:42.870
Okay.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.670
And these are the holders' quarters.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.940
When you're tired— err, are you tired?

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.670
Y-Y-Yeah.

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:54.690
Then how 'bout we take a rest in my room?

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:59.320
O-O-O-Oh, I think I'm fine! I'll manage!

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.110
You'll manage, huh?

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.470
Well, I mean, I'm not... b-b-but I will!

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:07.870
Nobunagun, you're so fun to tease!

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.850
Jess must've caught you off guard, huh.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.400
Oh! Uh... yeah.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:17.990
You probably won't believe this, 
but that's how she normally is.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.380
Wow, really?

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:25.660
It seems like, maybe because of the E-genes, 
some holders' personalities change.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:28.880
She's such an S in combat,

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:33.630
but off the battlefield she's the complete opposite, 
and... maybe because of a charitable disposition?

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:38.030
She tries to kiss any and 
everyone. Like, French kiss.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:42.580
Any and everyone? So those two aren't...

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:44.810
...dating?

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.500
You got a thing for Adam?

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.020
N-N-Not at all.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.250
You sure?

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.080
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:58.090
Well then, there's no reason for 
me to hesitate, is there?

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.130
Uh, uh, umm.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:03.150
I'm different off the battlefield, too.

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:06.180
I don't always play defense...

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.750
W-What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.020
Oops. Did I overdo it?

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:19.050
Did you learn anything, Vidocq?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:20.270
Yes.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:24.970
What you were saying the other day about 
something transmitting information,

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.940
we may be able to prove it.

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:28.670
Really?

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:34.020
I had John Hunter dissect 
the Florida Object...

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:37.840
...and there was a 
big opening in the brain.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:43.550
And in the video Galileo took of that landing 
ship self-destructing in Taiwan...

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:46.600
...here...

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:51.370
...all the scattering fragments 
register as Invasion Objects.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:55.040
Well, they are fragments of an Invasion 
Object, so even if they registered...

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:57.570
Yes, that's true.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:01.530
But these are coming back, 
however faintly, as alive.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:03.850
What are you saying?

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:09.030
Well, it's still just a hypothesis, but 
I have a way we can prove it.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.350
The difficulty level here is too high 
for a social life noob like me.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.810
Asao...

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.560
...Yeah. I gotta tough it out, huh.

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.280
No Net here either, huh?

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.780
<i>Atsumori,</i> that play... {TB: Since she repeats herself I clarify slightly Atsumori is the play she quoted as Nobunaga last ep.}

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.730
Aha! Here it is.

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:50.520
Man, I really did quote it line-for-line. {TB: Literally, "Man, it really is the same [as that time]..." but I really want people to get what she means.}

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:58.660
Has something inside me changed?

00:11:58.660 --> 00:11:59.810
Whatcha doin'?

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.710
Researching something?

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:04.020
Y-Yeah.

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.790
Don't be so cold!

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:10.260
Aren't we on the same platoon? 
You can tell me anything.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.220
Sure, but...

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:13.870
I want to support you, Sio.

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:16.050
I'm fine, though.

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:18.980
You don't have to hold back. 
Anything you need...

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:21.770
Too close, too close— 
her face is way too close!

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.120
I'll help you out with anything.

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:24.060
A-ny-thing.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:26.520
I can't do this!

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.740
I-I'm so sorry!

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:34.240
Well, I sure didn't expect <i>you</i> to come to me. 
Does this mean you're ready?

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:35.500
No, it doesn't!

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.500
Hmm! That's too bad.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.690
Umm... there's something 
I wanna ask you.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:46.340
The effects of E-genes?

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.170
I mean, how about you, Gandhi?

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:53.800
Hmm... I do think I've become a bit more 
amiable due to Gandhi's influence, but...

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:55.660
You were different before?

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.420
You wanna hear about it?

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.940
Not— I mean...

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.470
Incoming from the <i>Clayton Forrester!</i>

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:06.820
All Second Platoon holders are to 
report there immediately.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.810
Oh? Too bad.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:24.570
...The <i>Clayton Forrester?</i>

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:28.260
Yeah, the boat we were on up 
until this morning.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:31.770
Friggin' Vidocq. His plan sucks.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.330
Is that an Aquitaine?!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.750
<b>Aquitaine class
 French Navy Anti-submarine destroyer. {TB: Or "ASW destroyer" but "anti-submarine warefare destroyer" sounded kinda weird.}</b>

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:39.540
<b>Independence class
American Navy littoral combat ship.</b>

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.540
Even an Independence! This is nuts!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.050
Wow...

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.050
'Sup, Mr. Dai Zong?

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.190
'Lo.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.280
Even that little kid is a holder...

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:49.040
Oh, Miss Nobunagun. Nice work the other day!

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:50.220
Uh... who are you?

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.920
You don't remember?! How awful!

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.010
Umm...

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:56.450
Still don't know?

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:58.360
Oh! Back then!

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:00.760
Sheesh, you're just awful.

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:03.940
B-But, it sure is amazing that you're a 
holder as an elementary schooler.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:06.660
I am not an elementary schooler!!!

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.190
I-I-I'm sorry!

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:12.350
If you're gonna be like that, I'ma hafta 
discipline your newbie butt.

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:15.930
For starters, hmm...

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:20.850
Go to the kiosk and buy me yakisoba bread!

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:20.500
<b>Yakisoba bread </b>

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:22.870
Y-Yakisoba bread?

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.190
I've finally escaped the lowest 
rung of the social ladder!

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:28.990
My future is so bright!

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.180
And it's going straight to 
your head, I see.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.410
That voice— Mr. Jack.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:37.610
Yo.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.180
So Hunter's gopher has graduated?

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.460
I'm not a gopher!

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:46.260
I just buy stuff as a favor to him 
when I go for myself!

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:47.880
So you do buy stuff 
for him, huh.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:48.400
<b>Busted</b>

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:51.560
They call that being a "gopher." 

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.280
<b>Gopher 
 A person in a weaker position
 in a group used by a stronger 
person to run errands.</b>

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:54.660
<b>Gopher girl </b>

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:53.040
Yeah, I get that!

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.660
S-Sorry!

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.890
She doesn't want to admit it.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:00.650
Don't fight, kiddos. Get the frick along.

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:02.770
We're not kiddos!

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.550
Oh! Having fun?

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:07.970
N-N-N-Newton...

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:10.710
Happy to work with you today, Galileo.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.430
I-I've been injured...

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:22.100
 but the world... is still... turning... {TB: This is not in the script, but confident this is what she says.}

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.990
A-Are you okay?

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.100
Busy, busy, huh.

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:25.500
M-M-Mr. Vidocq!

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.230
So you're Nobunagun.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:28.970
Y-Yessir.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:32.320
I hear you performed admirably in Florida.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:34.590
I expect highly of you 
in this next operation.

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:35.820
Yessir!

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:40.160
Nobunagun! I won't forget this!

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.250
Man, she's been boring a hole in 
my back for a while...

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:47.120
There are two objectives in this mission.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:52.200
The first is the Easter Island armored destroyer 
Object that the Sixth Platoon let escape.

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:55.870
The second is to seize some of 
this Invasion Object's brain cells.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:16:00.120
Hey! You mean you're makin' us clean up 
after some other platoon?!

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:04.120
Well, there's not an infinite amount 
of holders, you know.

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:05.640
We have to help each other out.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:10.550
This is you talking, so this must 
be about the brain sample.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:17.060
I'm asking Dai Zong from the Third 
Platoon to secure the brain sample.

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:18.580
Understood.

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:24.020
As for the armored Object... 
Nobunagun, I'm having you take point.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.820
Got it! M-Me?!

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:31.330
Are you for real? 
That squirt Nobunagun over me?!

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:32.320
What a joke!

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:37.300
The commander chose the 
personnel for this mission.

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:38.800
What?!

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:45.080
This Invasion Object is covered in armor 
that even AU weapons cannot break.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.310
The only way to target its brain cells

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:50.600
is to hit this tiny crevice 
on the upper part of its neck.

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:54.680
Shooter Nobunagun seems more suited 
to that job than you, Jack.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.310
I guess so...

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:00.400
The commander picked me...

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.360
You'll get it done, right?

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:04.540
Yes! I'll do my best!

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:28.630
Observation to Mission Control. 
We've confirmed the target.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:31.770
One armored, five gunboats.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:37.950
If anything registers during my observation, 
it will be displayed in these goggles.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:41.730
And that's what we want 
you to chase down!

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:43.400
Understood!

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.150
Incoming report from the picket ship.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.930
There appear to be five gunboat Objects 
escorting the armored one from Easter Island.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:55.460
They've entered the operation zone!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:01.050
Operation is go.

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:03.560
Launching an all-out attack!

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:22.540
Don't hesitate! Fire!

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:36.990
One down!

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:44.210
Come at me.

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:45.600
Well?

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:50.020
It's no good. Those gunboat Objects aren't 
giving off the reaction we're looking for.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:52.090
So it has to be a flagship...

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.310
Is she gonna be okay?

00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:01.160
Oh, one way or another!

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.290
Gotta get it together. 
Get it together and aim straight.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.490
The crevice on the upper part of its neck...

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.790
I'll mop up the rest of these guys. 
You two, support her!

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:30.010
Ohhh?

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:31.740
So good of you to look 
out for the newbie.

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:33.370
Shaddup and go!

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:34.860
Aye aye!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:37.980
Now, then...

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.780
Don't get upset over one 
crummy underling.

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:48.830
Are you okay?

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.930
Gandhi, why are you—?

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:55.130
The request of a certain worrywort...

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.580
That's right.

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:00.760
Eat dirt! {TB: Literally "crawl" lol But obviously she'd be smashing it into the ground...if they were on the ground. It seems a little weird even in Japanese. I guess the dirt off the bottom of her shoe if nothing else ;D}

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.330
Finish it, Nobunagun!

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:05.660
Right!

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.990
Take this!

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:18.190
A reaction!

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:22.370
312 of 'em. Direction, speed...

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:25.770
There! Get it!

00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:27.140
Understood!

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:35.340
Tag!

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:39.640
And?

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:42.050
Got it!

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.360
Success!

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:49.810
We did it!

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:53.990
So...

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:55.660
It's just as I hypothesized.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:59.260
That Invasion Object is one that lives parasitically 
in another Invasion Object's brain.

00:20:59.890 --> 00:21:01.510
Please explain.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:02.910
Of course.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:07.470
This Invasion Object records the host 
Object's memories in its body.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:11.660
Upon the death of the host, 
it immediately jumps ship into the sea.

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:16.890
It can't be killed by an animal from Earth, 
so even if it gets eaten by a fish or something,

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:19.140
it lives on inside that body,

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:22.930
and travels via the food chain 
and animal migration.

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:26.970
That must be how they transmit 
news of a defeat.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:30.650
And a new Invasion Object 
will be born knowing that info.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:34.060
So there's a "messenger" class?

00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:40.780
The intense speed of the Invasion Objects' 
evolution is due to these messengers.

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:44.230
A terrifying fact.

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:49.210
If they keep evolving at 
this speed, humanity...

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:53.210
...could be supplanted.

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.250
Princess, you got your 
clothes all dirty again!

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:28.980
Cyx, you're just nitpicky!

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:30.960
Geronimo, you just don't care enough!

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:32.900
Gaudi, you dare admonish the princess?!

00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:34.240
You think you're so high and mighty!

00:23:35.170 --> 00:23:37.670
Next time, Gun No. 6: "Monster Meat."

00:23:37.670 --> 00:23:39.480
Sorry!
